            <ArticleTitle>Arachnoid cyst and arachnoiditis following idiopathic spinal subarachnoid haemorrhage.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>578-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02688690701832118</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe 8 years follow-up of a case of arachnoid cyst developing after spinal subarachnoid haemorrhage. The cyst was removed by hemilaminectomy; an arachnoid cyst of the same size was again observed by MRI 2 weeks later. We suggest that conservative approach could be the best choice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
